{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30136 - PROTEIN:5793",
  "verbalization": "Tigloylgomisin H appears to have a direct target relationship with Hepatocyte through multiple pathways, with the most consistent link being its interaction with VMRC-LCP, which is targeted by Cocosamide B and subsequently by Tigloylgomisin H. This suggests a potential mechanism where Tigloylgomisin H may act through a shared pathway involving VMRC-LCP, which in turn influences Hepatocyte function. The evidence from Path 1 and Path 3 supports this, as both pathways converge on VMRC-LCP as a target, with the latter pathway providing a more detailed molecular description of the target. The presence of multiple targets (MOVP-3 and the complex compound) further indicates that Tigloylgomisin H may exert its effects through diverse mechanisms, possibly by modulating different pathways that ultimately lead to Hepatocyte targeting. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, but the shared target VMRC-LCP provides a central point of connection.",
